[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "2607242000", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-* -- extend the ToSMonitor-LLM/ToSArchiveGovernor actor from the 1-repo pilot to a 10-repo validation batch", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/date "2026-07-24", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607241900-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-pilot.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607241800-cloud-itonami-commitment-ledger-actor-blueprint.edn"], :adr/scope-still-not-fleet-wide "this ADR extends the actor layer to 11 of ~155 cloud-itonami-lei-* repos total (the ADR-2607241900 pilot + these 10). The remaining ~144 repos are STILL untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300 -- this is an owner-approved validation batch (chosen explicitly over a full fleet-wide rewrite when asked), not a decision to convert the whole family. A further follow-up decision is required to go beyond this batch", :adr/batch-companies "cloud-itonami-lei-06btx5uwzd0gq5n5y745 (Westinghouse Air Brake Technologies Corporation, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-254900glqzad4n7n5q19 (Public Storage, US-MD), cloud-itonami-lei-5299004emj3r4rvr5y75 (東京電力ホールディングス株式会社/TEPCO, JP), cloud-itonami-lei-529900qbvwxmwanh7h45 (Siemens Healthineers AG, DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300ddu6fdrbiels05 (Fox Corporation, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300iglytzuk3pvp70 (WEC Energy Group Inc, US-WI), cloud-itonami-lei-549300szyinbbljqu475 (AerCap Holdings N.V., NL), cloud-itonami-lei-765lhxwgk1kxcltfyq30 (Pfizer Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-apvbkpoulhux7yzlku17 (Antero Resources Corporation, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-lh7mqb13nwy7cj9vc445 (Brookdale Senior Living Inc, US-DE) -- selected as an evenly-spread sample across the ~155-repo list (not cherry-picked for ease), spanning 4 jurisdictions (US/JP/DE/NL) and a range of industries (rail equipment, storage REIT, electric utility, medtech, media, energy utility, aircraft leasing, pharma, oil & gas, senior living)", :adr/identical-code-per-company "tosmonitor.governor/phase/operation/registry/advisor -- the six HARD checks, the phase gate, the StateGraph wiring, and the mock-advisor diff logic -- are BYTE-IDENTICAL across all 11 repos (this fleet's own 'reused, not shared code across the repo boundary' convention: copied deliberately, not require'd across repo boundaries, so each repo stays independently forkable). Only tosmonitor.store (company/baseline demo data), README.md, and docs/adr/0001 are company-specific", :adr/real-bug-found-doc-type-vocabulary "extending to this batch surfaced a real correctness bug in the pilot: tosmonitor.registry/known-doc-types (#{:terms-of-service :privacy-policy :cookie-policy :acceptable-use :other-legal}) was GUESSED, not grounded in real archive data -- a grep survey of :tos/doc-type across all 155 cloud-itonami-lei-* journal files found the real vocabulary is #{:terms-of-service :privacy-policy :terms-of-use :legal-notice :terms-of-carriage :terms-and-conditions :legal-disclaimer :vendor-terms-and-conditions :risk-disclosures :policies-and-guidelines :legal-hub :contract-of-carriage} -- none of the three guessed values (:cookie-policy/:acceptable-use/:other-legal) occur anywhere in the real family. Brookdale's own archive (:terms-of-use) would have false-positive HARD-held on the original guessed set. Fixed in the pilot repo (cloud-itonami-lei-2572ibtt8cczw6au4141 PR #2, merged before this batch started) and shipped correctly from the start in all 10 new repos", :adr/demo-baseline-is-short-synthetic-per-company "matching the pilot's own convention (ADR-2607241900): each repo's tosmonitor.store/demo-baseline uses a SHORT, hand-written representative excerpt (not the real, page-length archived full text) with a self-consistent SHA-256 computed from that excerpt itself at store-construction time -- but source-url/retrieved-at/doc-type/legal-name/website are each company's REAL values, read from that repo's own blueprint.edn and 80-data/public/tos.journal.edn", :adr/test-status-batch10 "each of the 10 repos independently passes its own governor contract (6 HARD checks + high-stakes/never-auto invariant), phase invariants, store parity (MemStore/DatomicStore), and advisor smoke tests, plus a clean clojure -M:dev:run walkthrough, before being merged -- same bar as the pilot, not a relaxed bulk-scaffold bar", :adr/body "# ADR-2607242000: cloud-itonami-lei-* ToSMonitor batch-of-10 extension\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607241900 (the 1-repo pilot this batch extends); ADR-2607110300\n  (the archive-only design still governing the other ~144 repos, unchanged).\n\n## Context\n\nADR-2607241900 landed a governed ToSMonitor-LLM/ToSArchiveGovernor actor on\nexactly one `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repo (P&G) as a pilot, explicitly leaving\n'extend further' as a follow-up decision requiring separate owner sign-off.\nThe owner asked to extend to the rest of the family in the same session. Given\nthe scale (~154 remaining repos, each requiring a real build+test+PR+merge),\nthe owner chose a 10-repo validation batch over converting the whole family at\nonce, and chose per-company manual construction (reading each repo's own\nreal `blueprint.edn`/`tos.journal.edn`, same rigor as the pilot) over a bulk\nauto-generation script.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **10 more repos, evenly sampled** across the ~155-repo list (not the\n   easiest/most convenient ones): Westinghouse Air Brake Technologies,\n   Public Storage, TEPCO (Tokyo Electric Power, the only non-US/EU\n   jurisdiction in this batch -- deliberately included to stress-test the\n   `source-domain-mismatch-violations` check against a `.co.jp` two-part-TLD\n   domain, a known naive-base-domain limitation already documented in\n   `tosmonitor.registry`), Siemens Healthineers, Fox Corporation, WEC Energy\n   Group, AerCap Holdings, Pfizer, Antero Resources, and Brookdale Senior\n   Living.\n2. **The actor code itself is copied byte-identical**, not re-derived, across\n   all 11 repos now carrying it -- `tosmonitor.governor`/`phase`/`operation`/\n   `registry`/`advisor` have zero company-specific content. Only\n   `tosmonitor.store`'s demo data, `README.md`, and `docs/adr/0001` differ per\n   repo. This matches this fleet's own established convention of\n   re-implementing shared logic locally per actor repo (so each stays\n   independently forkable) rather than a cross-repo `:local/root` dependency.\n3. **A real bug surfaced during this batch, fixed before any of the 10 new\n   repos shipped**: `tosmonitor.registry/known-doc-types` in the pilot was a\n   GUESSED set, not grounded in the archive family's actual data. A grep\n   survey across all 155 `tos.journal.edn` files found the real vocabulary,\n   and Brookdale's own archive (`:terms-of-use`) is a live example of a doc-\n   type the guessed set would have wrongly rejected. Fixed in the pilot\n   (separate small PR, tests re-verified green) before any of this batch's\n   10 repos were built, so all 10 ship with the corrected vocabulary from the\n   start.\n4. **Same bar as the pilot, no relaxed bulk threshold**: each of the 10 repos\n   gets its own governor-contract/phase/store-parity/advisor test suite, its\n   own `clojure -M:dev:run` walkthrough, and its own PR+merge -- verified\n   individually, not scaffolded and assumed correct.\n5. **Still not fleet-wide.** ~144 `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos remain\n   untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300. Whether to continue beyond\n   this batch is an explicit further decision, not implied by this ADR.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Validates the actor pattern holds up across genuinely different\n  companies/jurisdictions/domain shapes, not just the single pilot case --\n  and found a real cross-repo correctness bug (doc-type vocabulary) in the\n  process, which a 1-repo pilot alone could not have surfaced.\n- (+) The `.co.jp`/multi-part-TLD domain-matching limitation the pilot's own\n  `tosmonitor.registry` docstring already flagged as a known V1 gap is now\n  exercised against a real case (TEPCO) rather than only a hypothetical one.\n- (-) 11 of ~155 repos (about 7%) now carry this actor layer; the other 93%\n  remain plain archives. The coverage question is still mostly '0% governed'\n  fleet-wide.\n- (-) Byte-identical code duplicated across 11 repos means a future fix (like\n  the doc-type vocabulary one) must be backported to each repo individually\n  unless/until a shared-library extraction is decided separately.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607241900 (`90-docs/adr/2607241900-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-pilot.edn`)\n- ADR-2607110300 (`90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn`)\n- The 10 repos' own `docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md` records\n"}]
